# ::stuff tracks TeX Live's rolling tlnet archive, whose per-revision
# tarballs are DELETED upstream within days — by the time a synced ebuild
# reaches this image the distfile is a 404 on every CTAN mirror
# (texlive-luatex r79730, 2026-08-10: gone from tu-chemnitz and gust.org.pl
# alike, killed the whole post-kernel emerge). The installed ::pwr copies
# keep working and nothing in the image needs the newer snapshots; unmask
# deliberately after a sync if a texlive bump is actually wanted, and fetch
# the same day.
dev-texlive/*::stuff

# app-text/texlive-core is the same rot one category over: 2026-r3 pins
# texlive-scripts.r80004, and CTAN's tlnet/archive already rotated it out
# (2026-08-21: the mirror carries r80029 and r80039, nothing older), so every
# SRC_URI entry — gentoo mirrors, dev.gentoo.org, tu-chemnitz, CTAN — is a 404
# and the fetch cannot be repaired locally. The installed 2026-r1 keeps working
# even though ::stuff has since dropped its ebuild. Masking above r1 rather
# than the whole package leaves the older 2025 ebuild visible without letting
# --update pick it. Drop this line once ::stuff bumps to a live revision.
>app-text/texlive-core-2026-r1::stuff
